==Description== 

The [[Image:PartDesign_Revolution.svg|24px]] '''PartDesign Revolution''' tool creates a solid in the active Body by revolving a sketch, a 2D object, or one or more faces about a given axis. Its shape is combined with the existing solid if there are previous features.

[[File:PartDesign Revolution example.svg]]

{{Caption|Above: sketch (A) is revolved 270 degrees counter-clockwise around axis (B); resulting solid (C) is shown right.}}

==Usage==

# Select a single sketch or similar 2D object, or one or more faces from a single sketch or other object, or from the Body itself.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:PartDesign_Revolution.svg|16px]] [[PartDesign_Revolution|Revolve]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part Design → Additive Features → [[Image:PartDesign_Revolution.svg|16px]] Revolve}} option from the menu.
# The task panel opens.
# Set the parameters, see [[#Options|Options]] below. {{Version|1.1}}: If the {{MenuCommand|Show interactive draggers when editing features}} [[PartDesign_Preferences#General|preference]] is selected (default), angle parameters can be adjusted with interactive gizmos in the [[3D_View|3D View]].
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button to close the task panel and finish the tool.
# A Revolution feature appears under the active Body.

==Editing==

The Revolution can be edited after its creation in two ways:
* Double-clicking it in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]], or by right-clicking and selecting '''Edit Revolution''' in the context menu; this brings up the task panel and ({{Version|1.1}}) the interactive gizmos (if enabled).
* Via the [[Property_View|Property View]].

==Options==

The task panel offers the following settings:

[[Image:PartDesign_Revolution_Taskpanel.png|frame]]

===Start===

{{Version|26.3}}

Sets the angular starting position of the revolution around the axis. By default the revolution starts at the sketch or face used as its profile.
* '''Profile plane''' (default): the revolution starts directly at the profile's sketch plane or face.
* '''Offset''': the revolution starts at an angular offset from the profile, entered in the '''Offset''' field.
* '''Reference''': the revolution starts at a face, [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]], or sketch selected with the {{Button|Pick Reference}} button.

===Direction===

{{Version|26.3}}

Sets the direction(s) of the revolution:
* '''One sided''': the revolution extends on one side of the sketch or face.
* '''Two sided''': the revolution extends on both sides of the sketch or face. Two sub-menus (''Side 1'' and ''Side 2'') appear to define the revolution for each side.
* '''Symmetric''': the revolution is symmetrical with respect to the original sketch or face.

===Axis===

Specifies the axis of the revolution:
* '''Vertical sketch axis''': selects the vertical sketch axis.
* '''Horizontal sketch axis''': selects the horizontal sketch axis.
* '''Construction line''': selects a construction line from the sketch used by the revolution. The dropdown list will contain an entry for each construction line. The first construction line will be labelled ''Construction line 1''.
* '''Base (X/Y/Z)-axis''': selects the X-, Y- or Z-axis of the Body's origin.
* '''Select reference…''': allows the selection of a straight edge or a [[Part_DatumLine|datum line]] from the Body.

Note that when changing the axis, the '''Reversed''' option may be (un)checked automatically.

===Type===

{{Version|1.0}}

''For Side 1 and Side 2 if applicable.''

Offers four ways to specify the angle of the revolution:
* '''Angle''': enter a numeric value for the '''Angle''' of the revolution. With the '''Direction''' option '''Symmetric''' the revolution will extend half the given angle to either side of the sketch or face.
* '''To last''': the revolution will extend up to the last face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.
* '''To first''': the revolution will extend up to the first face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.
* '''Up to face''': the revolution will extend up to a face. Press the {{Button|Face}} button and select a face or a [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]] from the Body.

===Angle===

''For Side 1 and Side 2 if applicable.''

Defines the angle of the revolution. This option is only available if '''Type''' (for the same side) is '''Angle'''. Angles larger than 360° are not possible.

===Project selected axis to profile plane===

{{Version|26.3}}

Projects the selected axis onto the profile plane if the profile is planar (only available for planar profiles). When unchecked (default), the axis is used in its original position and direction.

===Reversed===

Reverses the direction of the revolution.

===Recompute on change===

This option should be checked if '''Show final result''' or '''Show preview overlay''' is checked.

===Show final result===

If checked the cumulative result of the previous features and the current operation is shown.

===Show preview overlay===

If checked the result of the current operation is shown as an overlay.

==Properties==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

A PartDesign Revolution object is derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part Feature]] object and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:

===Data===

{{TitleProperty|Compatibility}}

* {{PropertyData|Fuse Order|Enumeration|Hidden}}: {{Version|1.1}}

{{TitleProperty|Part Design}}

See [[PartDesign_Pad#Data|PartDesign Pad]].

{{TitleProperty|Revolution}}

* {{PropertyData|Side Type|Enumeration}}: {{Value|One side}}, {{Value|Two sides}} or {{Value|Symmetric}}. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Base|Vector|ReadOnly}}: The axis base point derived from the {{PropertyData|Reference Axis}}.
* {{PropertyData|Axis|Vector|ReadOnly}}: The axis vector derived from the {{PropertyData|Reference Axis}}.
* {{PropertyData|Project Axis|Bool}}: If checked, the {{PropertyData|Reference Axis}} is projected onto the profile plane. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Reference Axis|LinkSub}}: Reference to the axis of the revolution.

{{TitleProperty|Side1}}

* {{PropertyData|Type|Enumeration}}: {{Value|Angle}}, {{Value|UpToLast}}, {{Value|UpToFirst}} or {{Value|UpToFace}}. Do not use {{Value|?TwoAngles}}. Defines how the revolution will end.
* {{PropertyData|Angle|Angle}}: The angle of the revolution.
* {{PropertyData|Up To Face|LinkSub}}: Face where the revolution will end.
* {{PropertyData|Up To Shape|LinkSubList}}: Not used.

{{TitleProperty|Side2}}

The properties in this group are only editable if {{PropertyData|Side Type}} is {{Value|Two sides}}. See the '''Side1''' group for more information about the properties.

* {{PropertyData|Type2|Enumeration}}: {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Angle2|Angle}}
* {{PropertyData|Up To Face2|LinkSub}}:  {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Up To Shape2|LinkSubList}}:  {{Version|1.1}}

{{TitleProperty|Sketch Based}}

See [[PartDesign_Pad#Data|PartDesign Pad]].

{{TitleProperty|Start}}

See [[PartDesign_Pad#Data|PartDesign Pad]].


